  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pennsylvania has $654M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Award activity shows 1,963 awards with an average award size of $333K. Obligations fell 97.7% year over year. Fiscal-year context shows a multi-year high in FY25 at $30.1B, followed by $28.3B in FY26 and the current FY27 total of $654M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry in FY2027 to date with $375M in obligations. The Department of Energy is the largest buying agency in FY2027 to date with $372M in obligations. FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $373M in obligations. This snapshot highlights where federal dollars flowed in the state during the fiscal-year-to-date period.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 spending compare with prior years?",
        "body": "Pennsylvania had $654M in obligations in FY2027 to date compared with $28.3B in FY26 and $30.1B in FY25. Obligations fell 97.7% year over year. FY24 registered $29.8B, FY23 registered $27.1B, and FY22 registered $20.8B. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is the largest buyer with $372M in obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $220M. FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC is the largest vendor with $373M in obligations, followed by RICHARD GROUP LLC with $64.9M and SERVIAM CONSTRUCTION LLC with $34.3M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the top industry with $375M in obligations."
      }
